BT 1 0 0 1 0 75.5 Tm 12 TL /F2 8.5 Tf .117647 .160784 .231373 rg (1.4 Why Are Infrared Observations Important?) Tj /F1 8.5 Tf  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 8.5 Tf (Piercing Interstellar Dust:) Tj /F1 8.5 Tf ( Cosmic dust clouds absorb and scatter visible light, hiding young stars and galactic centers. Longer) Tj T* (infrared wavelengths glide straight through dust grains.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 8.5 Tf (Detecting Cold Matter:) Tj /F1 8.5 Tf ( Low-mass brown dwarfs, planetary atmospheres, and interstellar ices radiate thermal energy almost) Tj T* (exclusively in the infrared.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 8.5 Tf (Cosmic Redshift:) Tj /F1 8.5 Tf ( Light emitted by infant galaxies in the early universe has been stretched into infrared bands by the cosmic) Tj T* (expansion of space over billions of years.) Tj T* ET
